    "summary": "Wired \u00a79's fruit into MatchRoom. pedestalSites puts one pedestal on each regular island at its highest-id dock (4). The deal comes from deriveSeed('fruit'), with a test-only pin (PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_FRUITS). stepFruits runs each world tick after the encounters and ruin presence, before the holds and the claim. Protocol v9: F is Buttons.Fruit, plus inspect-fruit / fruit-kit (reply to the inspector only, strict zod), per-client pedestal markers (full or empty, in sight) and the player's own kit, progress and last result in their status. Every sea duel's DuelMachine gets both kits: they are fixed in the frame-0 state and synced in the lobby's kits field, and both clients build the same state from them. Web: fruit panel (F inspects, holding F eats, progress ring, every refusal and interruption reason), HUD kit line, duel HUD kits, arena drawing model from fighterTells (bolts, smoke zones, obscured startup flash, reappearance, threats only for striking moves), pedestal markers on the sea. Ruins P2 items: the panel keydown router skips text fields, a Digit1-6 vs tablet-order test, an exact lockout test, and an open-water test; row 20 is now removed. Docs: architecture 'Fruits in the room', duel.md note, README. Branch table docs/fruit-kits-online-coverage.md: 135 rows (116 tested, 8 equivalent, 11 removed), built by deleting each branch on scratch copies outside the repo. Checks run on the final code: npm ci at the start; typecheck OK; test:unit 1352/1352; test:integration 124/124 in 177 s; build and smoke OK; full Playwright suite 14/14 with the JSON report, which check-report accepts (fruit-duel included).",
